every activity maps to a

116
00:11:54.667 --> 00:11:59.000
supplied requirement, and schedule
conflicts are flagged. Preference: use

117
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.333
plain language. Missing-information rule:
ask if the start date or

118
00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:07.667
required roles are absent; otherwise mark
unknown availability rather than

119
00:12:07.667 --> 00:12:12.000
inventing it. Verification: the team lead
checks mappings and schedule

120
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.333
against the originals. Notice that the
example is reusable because

121
00:12:16.333 --> 00:12:20.667
its decisions are labeled. A different
user can replace the

122
00:12:20.667 --> 00:12:25.000
bracketed inputs without rediscovering the
contract.

